  "goodToKnow": "Der Zivildienst was the alternative civilian service for conscientious objectors to military service, typically in hospitals, care homes and social services; the young men were called Zivis. When conscription (die Wehrpflicht) was suspended in 2011, Zivildienst ended too and was replaced by the voluntary Bundesfreiwilligendienst (Bufdi). For decades, Zivis were a pillar of the care sector. It has no plural."
